    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0291" n="187" xml:id="pg187"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3898: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-02T23:00:00+08:00">February 2, 1932—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 3—2:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 12, February 1, 3 p.m. [to Peck.] I arrived Nanking this afternoon and saw
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs 5 o’clock to whom Peck had just
                    delivered Department’s message.</p>
                <p>Lo showed me fragments of shells which he
                    stated had fallen on Lion Hill and on Pei Chi Ko where Soong has house.</p>
                <p>Saw Soong this evening. He said American
                    note gives them hope although he does not believe Japanese will accept. He
                    expects to go to Shanghai tomorrow to persuade bankers to give him money.</p>
                <p>French Minister received his instruction about 8 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
